cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this case study or its data in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "claude-mem in Production: A 70-Day Case Study of Distributed LLM Memory Infrastructure"
authors:
  - given-names: Alessandro
    alias: alessandropcostabr
    website: "https://github.com/alessandropcostabr"
abstract: >-
  A 70-day production study of claude-mem, a persistent memory plugin for
  Claude Code, running across a 3-machine fleet. The study documents 22,718
  structured observations, 987 automated benchmarks across 21 Claude Code
  versions, and a complete vector backend migration from Chroma to Qdrant.
  Continuous canary measurements independently corroborate the Anthropic
  March-April 2026 Claude Code performance regression and reveal a previously
  unreported divergence between Opus 4.6 and Haiku 4.5 on the same vendor
  harness. Four classes of silent failure are cataloged with reproduction
  details, and the total infrastructure cost is reported at approximately
  $225-$295. All aggregated data, scripts, and diagrams are released under
  CC-BY-4.0 for independent reproduction.
keywords:
  - LLM
  - claude-code
  - claude-mem
  - vector retrieval
  - canary benchmarking
  - silent failures
  - production observability
  - developer tools
  - prompt caching
